# --- Fix #10: security gap from the original review ---
# The original .gitignore only excluded /.vscode, /archi.txt, and itself.
# .env was NOT excluded (currently holds placeholder text, but nothing
# stopped a real password being committed the moment someone filled it in).
# inventory.yaml and monitor_thresholds.yaml contain real internal
# management IPs and were committed to a public repo. Generated capture
# output can contain real device state, IPs, and topology detail and was
# never excluded either. All of that is fixed below.

# Credentials -- never track this file. Copy .env.example to .env locally.
.env

# Real device inventory / thresholds -- contain real IPs. Track the
# .example versions instead and keep your real, filled-in copies local-only.
inventory.yaml
monitor_thresholds.yaml

# Generated capture output, reports, and logs
captures/
diff_report*.json
evaluation_report.json
report_*.html
report_*.md
pir_package_*/
triggers.log
monitor_logs/

# Standard Python housekeeping
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
venv/
.venv/

# Editor / misc (kept from the original file)
/.vscode
/archi.txt